# Go tooling (gofmt, go vet) expects LF. Without this, cloning on Windows with
# the default core.autocrlf=true gives a CRLF working tree and `gofmt -l .`
# lists every file in the repo: the project failing its own documented bar
# before the reviewer has read a line of code.
#
# text=auto lets git detect and skip binary files; eol=lf pins the working-tree
# ending for everything it does treat as text, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
